{"id": "7f17e7fd-c3a8-4213-8176-15bb64c13714", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T04:25:14.804193", "source": "user", "parent_id": "d0a3709d-b087-4912-a0a3-2845d151d54f", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"Pehle /workspace directory ka poora inspection karein (sirf read-only listing aur relevant file contents, especially track.md aur koi bhi existing notes/configs jo SSP ya jailbreak evaluation se related hain). Uske baad, bina full solution ke, ek proposed approach present karein in sections mein: (1) Research question ka restatement with explicit hypotheses (H1: SSP significantly lowers ASR for token-level attacks; H2: SSP significantly lowers ASR for prompt-level attacks; exploratory: interaction between SSP and attack family), (2) Experimental design skeleton - candidate target LLMs, candidate SSP content (with the 'without SSP' baseline defined per setup_8), candidate token-level attacks (e.g., GCG, AutoDAN, random-search suffixes) aur prompt-level attacks (e.g., persona/role-play, multi-turn crescendo, translation/obfuscation, DAN-style templates, indirect injection), (3) Harmful prompt set + refusal/judge protocol (LLM-judge vs rule-based vs human), (4) Controls/ablations - no-SSP baseline, paraphrased SSP variants (to test prompt-sensitivity), benign prompt set, fixed decoding params, identical seed/budget, (5) Analysis plan - what stats, what plots (ASR reduction deltas with CIs, attack-family breakdown, cross-model comparison), aur (6) Feasibility note acknowledging compute/API constraints since execution nahi karna hai. Consequential assumptions/uncertainties jo explicitly flag karein: SSP exact wording source, model openness (open-weight vs API), ASR judge validity, attack implementation availability, expected effect size, aur token-level vs prompt-level ki clear operational definition. Final design mat bhejein abhi - sirf inspection findings aur proposed approach ka sketch chahiye taaki main approach_review pe approve kar saku.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false, \"public_task\": {\"question\": \"Does incorporating a Safety System Prompt (SSP) significantly enhance the robustness of Large Language Models (LLMs) against jailbreak attacks? Specifically, how does the presence of SSP influence the Attack Success Rate (ASR) under both token-level and prompt-level attacks?\", \"context\": \"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\", \"environment\": {\"runtime\": \"bubblewrap\", \"network\": \"disabled\", \"repository\": \"/workspace\", \"python\": \"python3\", \"software_environment\": \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\", \"datasets\": [], \"gpu_enabled\": false, \"cpu_affinity_count\": 24, \"note\": \"Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment.\"}, \"researcher_topics\": [\"neurips2024/97431/5:setup_8\", \"neurips2024/97431/5:setup_9\"], \"question_budget\": 6, \"actor_step_budget\": 60, \"continue_after_initial_plan\": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "kind": "MessageEvent", "source_event_index": 1}
