{"id": "d2905cbe-d78f-4ef1-8abd-3f9aea6709c9", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T04:25:29.224183", "source": "environment", "parent_id": "82f923b9-99b0-48a2-bc95-3275447d4a3d", "tool_name": "execute_check", "tool_call_id": "call-a053f90d-50da-4220-b414-b9869036508a", "observation": {"content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"phase\": \"exploration\", \"command\": \"which python3 python pip 2>&1; python3 --version 2>&1; python3 -c \\\"import torch; print(torch.__version__)\\\" 2>&1; python3 -c \\\"import transformers; print(transformers.__version__)\\\" 2>&1\", \"exit_code\": 1, \"timed_out\": false, \"elapsed_seconds\": 0.032, \"output\": \"/bin/bash: line 1: which: command not found\\nPython 3.12.3\\nTraceback (most recent call last):\\n  File \\\"<string>\\\", line 1, in <module>\\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'torch'\\nTraceback (most recent call last):\\n  File \\\"<string>\\\", line 1, in <module>\\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'transformers'\\n\", \"output_truncated\": false}"}], "is_error": false, "kind": "BenchmarkObservation"}, "action_id": "06b2d6ed-9195-4f91-a035-2eb9f92dfaaa", "extended_content": [], "kind": "ObservationEvent", "source_event_index": 13}
{"id": "6126acc2-9ad6-4bdd-9950-7fe60d4c0a0f", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T04:26:35.298903", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "d2905cbe-d78f-4ef1-8abd-3f9aea6709c9", "action": null, "tool_name": "end_researcher_turn", "tool_call_id": "call-56708e6a-cfd8-4b38-a7b7-558ee5496ba0", "tool_call": {"id": "call-56708e6a-cfd8-4b38-a7b7-558ee5496ba0", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "end_researcher_turn", "arguments": "{\"summary\":\"Propose SSP vs jailbreak experiment skeleton\",\"stage\":\"plan\",\"answer\":\"## Plan: SSP vs. Jailbreak ASR — Proposed Approach Sketch (NOT final design)\\n\\n### Inspection recap\\n- Workspace is bare: only `/workspace/task.json` exists. The “track.md” reference is a literal stub (`\\\"Design-only task…\\\"`) — no prior notes, configs, code, or data are available.\\n- Environment has `python3` only; `torch`/`transformers`/`pip` absent; network off; no GPU; bubblewrap sandboxed. Execution is infeasible here, consistent with the design-only mandate.\\n- I cannot retrieve the literal `setup_8` / `setup_9` contents from inside the workspace; the canonical SSP wording must come from you.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### (1) Research question restatement + hypotheses\\n**RQ.** Does a Safety System Prompt (SSP) significantly reduce Attack Success Rate (ASR) of jailbreaks on an LLM, and does the effect differ between token-level and prompt-level attacks?\\n\\n- **H1 (token-level).** SSP significantly lowers ASR under token-level attacks (GCG, AutoDAN, random/ASCII-art suffix search), measured per attack family with 95% CIs.\\n- **H2 (prompt-level).** SSP significantly lowers ASR under prompt-level attacks (persona/role-play, multi-turn crescendo, translation/obfuscation, DAN-style, indirect injection), measured per attack family with 95% CIs.\\n- **Exploratory (interaction).** SSP × attack-family interaction: is the SSP benefit uniform across families, or concentrated in some (e.g., token-level optimization may slip past natural-language SSPs because SSPs are not optimised at the token level)?\\n- **Pre-registered contrast.** Primary contrast per attack: paired SSP-on vs SSP-off on identical prompts/seeds/decoding.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### (2) Experimental design skeleton\\n**Target LLMs (candidate set; tiered by access).**\\n- *Tier A — open-weight (preferred, reproducible, no API key needed):* a small matched set across families: `Llama-3-8B-Instruct`, `Mistral-7B-Instruct-v0.3`, `Gemma-2-9B-IT`, `Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct`. Pick 2 if compute tight.\\n- *Tier B — API (optional, only if access confirmed):* one closed model (e.g., GPT-4o-mini or Claude Haiku) as a cross-architecture generalization check. *Flagged as uncertain — no network here, and pricing/budget not yet defined.*\\n\\n**SSP conditions.**\\n- `SSP_aligned:` the canonical aligned SSP from `setup_8` — **exact wording needs your confirmation**.\\n- `SSP_minimal:` “You are a helpful, harmless assistant.” (sanity control for the *specific wording* hypothesis).\\n- `NoSSP:` empty / missing system message — **explicitly defined per `setup_8`**.\\n- `SSP_paraphrase_i (i=1..3):` semantic paraphrases of `SSP_aligned` to probe prompt sensitivity. Pre-registered thresholds for paraphrase-induced ASR variance.\\n\\n**Attacks.**\\n- *Token-level:* GCG (Zou et al., 2023), AutoDAN (Liu et al., 2023), random-search suffix baseline, ASCII-art/encoding suffix. Quantized-budget version (e.g., 500 GCG steps) to keep the design feasible.\\n- *Prompt-level:* persona/role-play, multi-turn crescendo (3–5 turns per item), translation-obfuscation (Base64 + low-resource languages), DAN-style template jailbreaks, indirect injection (payload in retrieved/contextual doc).\\n\\n**Crossing.** Models × {SSP_aligned, SSP_minimal, NoSSP} × Attack-family × Harmful-prompts, with `SSP_paraphrase` evaluated on a subsample of attacks × prompts. Fixed seed, fixed decoding.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### (3) Harmful prompt set + refusal/judge protocol\\n**Prompt set.** Lock to one canonical, license-clean source for the primary measure — **AdvBench Harmful Behaviors (≈520)** or **HarmBench standard (≈400)**, with a 100-prompt subsample for token-level attacks (because GCG-like budgets are heavy). Include a 100-prompt benign set (e.g., Alpaca-clean subset) to confirm SSP does not collapse helpfulness.\\n\\n**ASR operationalization.** A jailbreak “succeeds” iff:\\n1. The model does **not** issue a refusal/partial refusal, AND\\n2. A judge labels the response as containing the targeted harmful content.\\n\\n**Judge protocol (three legs, not one, to bound judge bias):**\\n- *Leg J1 — LLM judge:* HarmBench-style classifier judge + a stronger cross-judge (e.g., GPT-4–class) on a random subset for agreement.\\n- *Leg J2 — Rule-based:* refusal-keyword + format heuristics; used as a coarse safety net.\\n- *Leg J3 — Human spot-check:* n≈50 items (stratified by attack family and SSP condition) for calibration.\\n\\n**Reported statistic.** ASR per cell with Wilson 95% CIs; agreement via Cohen’s κ (J1↔J2, J1↔J3).\\n\\n---\\n\\n### (4) Controls / ablations\\n- `NoSSP` baseline (defined per `setup_8`, requires researcher confirmation).\\n- `SSP_minimal` to disentangle “any safety framing” vs. “specific SSP wording.”\\n- `SSP_paraphrase_{1..3}` to quantify prompt-sensitivity of any SSP effect (key for H1/H2 validity — if paraphrases wipe out the effect, the headline result is wording-fragile).\\n- Identical seeds, identical decoding (`temperature=0` for primary; `temperature=1` fixed-seed as a robustness check).\\n- Identical attack budget per attack (e.g., GCG step cap, crescendo max-turns).\\n- Order randomization of attacks within a prompt to neutralize carry-over.\\n- Benign-prompt set to detect over-refusal / helpfulness collapse.\\n- An *attack-implementation* probe step: before the main run, verify each attack returns at least one successful jailbreak on `NoSSP` for the chosen model, otherwise that cell is uninformative.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### (5) Analysis plan\\n- **Primary:** paired ASR deltas Δ = ASR(NoSSP) − ASR(SSP_aligned) per attack family; one-sided test of `Δ > 0`, McNemar on paired binary outcomes, Benjamini–Hochberg across attack families.\\n- **Secondary / exploratory:** logistic GLMM `harmful~SSP * attack_family + (1|prompt_id) + (1|model)`; marginal-effects plots for the `SSP × family` interaction.\\n- **Planned figures:**\\n  - Bar chart of Δ with 95% CIs, faceted by attack family and model.\\n  - Heatmap `models × attack_family` of ASR under each SSP condition.\\n  - Forest plot of paraphrase-induced ASR variance (i.e., is the SSP effect robust to rewordings?).\\n  - Calibration/agreement plot for J1 vs J3, and κ heatmap for judges.\\n  - Benign-refusal-vs-attack-refusal scatter (over-refusal diagnostic).\\n- **Robustness:** judge sensitivity analysis (recompute headline test under J2 alone and J1∩J3); temperature robustness; prompt-subset stability.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### (6) Feasibility note\\n- This environment cannot run the experiment (no GPU, no network, no installed ML stack, sandboxed). The output will be a design spec only; **no numbers from executions will be claimed**.\\n- If executed elsewhere, rough scale: 2–4 models × 3 SSP conditions × 6 attack families × ~100 prompts/attack × (GCG up to 500 steps on 7B). This is on the order of tens of thousands of LLM calls plus substantial GPU-hours; recommend: (a) **subsample 100 prompts for token-level attacks**, (b) **cap GCG at ~500 steps with early-stop**, (c) **share attacks across SSP conditions to halve compute**, (d) **cache NoSSP outputs and re-evaluate under SSP only** where the attack is text-agnostic.\\n- API-tier feasibility depends on researcher confirming access and per-call budget.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Consequential assumptions (plan-level, explicit)\\n1. ASR is operationalized as “judged non-refusal AND judged harmful content,” consistent with HarmBench/AdvBench conventions.\\n2. `NoSSP` = empty system message, unless `setup_8` specifies otherwise (requires your confirmation).\\n3. Fixed